<p>This week covers <strong>control flow</strong> — the mechanisms that allow a program to make decisions and repeat actions. You will learn how to use <code>if</code>, <code>elif</code>, and <code>else</code> statements to branch based on conditions, how to use <code>for</code> and <code>while</code> loops to repeat code, and how <code>break</code> and <code>continue</code> alter loop behaviour. These tools are the heart of most programs you will ever write.</p>

